      "title": "Projected plate area does the work",
      "description": "Settling depends on surface area. Each inclined plate adds its horizontal projected area, so a lamella clarifier provides many times the settling area of a conventional clarifier of the same footprint. Particles only fall a few centimetres to the plate, then slide down into the hopper while clarified water flows up between the plates to the launders.",
